    "publication_date": "2026-07-06",
    "description": "<p>This record preserves the interlanguage and constructed-language methodology sidecar for the Modern LaTeX Manuscripts project: Interslavic and Slavic translation governance, weighted automaton and term-weight ledgers, CJK/Arabic/RTL/Persianate source-body support packages, and Claude/ChatGPT/Fable provenance materials.</p>\n<p><strong>Read first:</strong> <code>00_Interlanguage_Methodology_Current_20260706.pdf</code>. The main payloads are grouped rather than scattered: full provenance, Interslavic weighted automaton and term ledgers, and source-body baseline transfer packages.</p>\n<p><strong>Status caveat.</strong> This is methodology and corpus infrastructure, not a certified language edition, not native-speaker approval, and not proof that any language branch is complete. Generated draft material may propose terms and expose inconsistencies, but source-body and independent/native witness status must remain separate from generated translation status.</p>\n<p><strong>GitHub.</strong> Corrections, added source bodies, better weighting heuristics, and cleaned language-branch packages can be suggested via issues or pull requests at <a href=\"https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts\">https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts</a>.</p>",
